The same suite update also rewrote timeline_browser_probe_test.go, undoing
c64b1ad exactly — REQ-178's deterministic fixture for
TestBrowserBehaviorTimelineProseDescribesOnlyTheWindowOnScreen. With the
strict browser lane running again, that left the gate red on the same
hardcoded late-July window that no longer contains live archive rows, and
every other REQ's canonical gate inherits the failure.

Re-apply c64b1ad's Route A fixture verbatim; it reverse-applies cleanly, so
the update contributed nothing of its own to this file.

Verified: `QUEUE_KANBAN_BROWSER=... go test -run
'^TestMaintainerStrictBrowserBehaviorLane$'` is green in 81s, red before.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
